<h2>A substantial market with a materially different operating picture since 2022</h2>
<p>Russia is, in the trade data we've verified, a genuinely significant destination for Indian guar gum and groundnut kernels, with smaller volumes of dehydrated onion and fresh grapes also moving. We're not going to present this lane as business-as-usual, though — international sanctions on Russian banking since 2022 have materially complicated standard payment routing, and shipping routes have generally become longer and less direct than they were before.</p>

<h2>What we actually do differently here</h2>
<p>Rather than quoting standard LC or TT terms and hoping they clear, we have a direct conversation with each Russia-bound buyer about a currently workable payment mechanism before booking anything. The same applies to routing and realistic transit time — we confirm what's actually achievable at the time of your enquiry rather than quoting a fixed pre-2022 baseline.</p>

<h2>Guar gum's specific requirement</h2>
<p>Guar gum shipments into Russia carry a documented requirement for pre-shipment quality certification from an approved testing laboratory — a standard, verifiable part of the documentation package we prepare for this route, not an obstacle that should surprise a buyer mid-order.</p>

